{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>To bind</b> — After he was bound, he reached a great height, to bind Pharaoh's officers without Pharaoh's counsel, but only by the counsel of his own soul." "<b>And his elders</b> — That Pharaoh's elders were with him as disciples before him." "<b>He will make wise</b> — Like 'and the fowl of the heaven will tell us' (Job 35:11), meaning he will teach them wisdom hidden from them."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 105, :notes {0 "Resolved ambiguous referent: 'his own soul' refers to Joseph's, not Pharaoh's, based on context.", 1 "Pronoun 'him' refers to Joseph throughout."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:38:28.116012080Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}